%p.mb-3
  The Tree Widget requires jQuery. Load jQuery on your page before the widget script below.

%p.mb-3
  Add these stylesheet and script tags to your HTML page's
  %code= '<head>'
  section:
%pre.bg-light.border.rounded.p-3
  %code
    = preserve do
      :escaped
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="#{request.base_url}/widgets/jquery.ncbo.tree.css">
        <script src="#{request.base_url}/widgets/jquery.ncbo.tree-2.0.2.js"></script>

%h6.mt-4 Add the tree to your page
%p.mb-3
  Paste this code into your HTML page where you want the class tree for #{@ontology.acronym} to appear:
%pre.bg-light.border.rounded.p-3
  %code
    = preserve do
      :escaped
        <div id="widget_tree"></div>
        <script>
          jQuery(function($) {
            $("#widget_tree").NCBOTree({
              apikey: "YOUR_API_KEY",
              ontology: #{@ontology.acronym.to_json},
              ncboUIURL: #{request.base_url.to_json},
              ncboAPIURL: #{$REST_URL.to_json}
            });
          });
        </script>

%p.mb-3
  Replace
  %code YOUR_API_KEY
  with your #{$SITE} API key. To display a different ontology, change the
  %code ontology
  value to that ontology's acronym.

%p.mb-3
  The
  %code widget_tree
  ID connects the container to the initialization code. If you rename it, also update the
  %code #widget_tree
  selector in the script.

%p.mb-3
  See the
  = link_to('detailed demonstration', '/widgets/ncbo_tree.html', target: '_blank')
  for examples of handling class selection and tree events.
%p.mb-0
  For more help visit the
  = succeed '.' do
    = link_to('NCBO Wiki', 'https://www.bioontology.org/wiki/NCBO_Widgets#NCBO_Ontology_Tree_Widget', target: '_blank')
